      "content": "it's not just \"shifting climates\" though. i did a side-by-side on some of the devotion and dissent-related texts and the metadata isn't just \"different\"—it's missing entirely in certain blocks, like the words were pulled from the index before the scan even happened. it’s too clean to be a coincidence. it’s almost like the concept itself is being scrubbed from the record so people can't even search for it anymore. if someone wanted to rewrite history, this is exactly how they'd do it, right? by making the ability to even name the idea disappear.",
